{"items":[{"owner":{"account_id":3674367,"reputation":72549,"user_id":9327,"user_type":"registered","accept_rate":50,"profile_image":"https://i.sstatic.net/jlp4Q.png?s=256","display_name":"anongoodnurse","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/9327/anongoodnurse"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1660651159,"post_id":42847,"comment_id":91626,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"I want you to get an answer, I really do, but this question is likely to attract answers without reliable sources. Is there any reason you haven&#39;t discussed this with the child&#39;s doctor? If you have, what did they say? They are most likely to be in the best position to answer this question. If you have a specific reason for asking here rather than  taking your doctor&#39;s advice, please edit your question and include it. Thanks."},{"owner":{"account_id":26070298,"reputation":21,"user_id":43411,"user_type":"unregistered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/3a1680a6d485c1bbf764c3ebad5e3002?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"Evina","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/43411/evina"},"reply_to_user":{"account_id":3674367,"reputation":72549,"user_id":9327,"user_type":"registered","accept_rate":50,"profile_image":"https://i.sstatic.net/jlp4Q.png?s=256","display_name":"anongoodnurse","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/9327/anongoodnurse"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1660723730,"post_id":42847,"comment_id":91630,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"The baby is not born yet. We are now just investigating how to approach this problem. We tried to look for general medical advice online (i.e., official channels of hospitals and medical practitioners), but haven&#39;t seen anyone addressing this specific issue of contaminated water. We are, naturally, intending to consult with the ob-gyn during the next visit, but also think they may not have an advice (they are not familiar with our water situation). That is why we were wondering whether others had a similar dilemma and how they tackled it."},{"owner":{"account_id":3674367,"reputation":72549,"user_id":9327,"user_type":"registered","accept_rate":50,"profile_image":"https://i.sstatic.net/jlp4Q.png?s=256","display_name":"anongoodnurse","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/9327/anongoodnurse"},"edited":false,"score":1,"creation_date":1660739793,"post_id":42847,"comment_id":91631,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"OB-GYNs are not going to have answers, as they don&#39;t do child care. Find out who your baby&#39;s pediatrician will be (if you don&#39;t know already); they are the one with which to speak. Your problem is fairly localized and even you do not know specifically what is in your water. I doubt we can do better than a local doctor."},{"owner":{"account_id":26064021,"reputation":81,"user_id":43409,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/9e46c6ae53eb059ed899aac5972c272f?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"Rachel","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/43409/rachel"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1660749413,"post_id":42844,"comment_id":91632,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"Thank you for the responses. I am a first time mom and I try to have reasonable expectations but am not always sure what is reasonable vs what is enabling him to always get what he wants (getting down right away instead of sitting longer). My in-laws/his grandparents make a lot of negative comments about how he’s “always busy” “can’t sit still” things like that. He’s following in the footsteps of their other grandson who’s a year older and liked sitting at the table for long periods of time. So, I’m at a loss of how to respond."},{"owner":{"account_id":9197749,"reputation":2046,"user_id":26398,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://i.sstatic.net/SzmpQ.jpg?s=256","display_name":"Pyrotechnical","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/26398/pyrotechnical"},"edited":false,"score":1,"creation_date":1660944114,"post_id":42847,"comment_id":91642,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"A pediatrician actually may not be the sole source you should inquire about on this. Can you clarify where you are that non-potable water is being sent to your house? For the US, the potability of water delivered to your house is usually regulated by on the state level. If you&#39;re on well water, the well driller is typically responsible for certifying the potability of the water being pumped. Can you further clarify what the impediments are to getting the water testing? The specific nature of the contamination will directly affect what needs to be done to render the water potable."},{"owner":{"account_id":3674367,"reputation":72549,"user_id":9327,"user_type":"registered","accept_rate":50,"profile_image":"https://i.sstatic.net/jlp4Q.png?s=256","display_name":"anongoodnurse","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/9327/anongoodnurse"},"edited":false,"score":1,"creation_date":1662502645,"post_id":42868,"comment_id":91698,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"Is it possible (please keep an open mind here) that he&#39;s <i>not</i> doing it for attention, but that it&#39;s a self-stimulating activity that he enjoys? &quot;Look!&quot;, he giggles, &quot;Look at the power I have over my body! Isn&#39;t it <i>amazing?!!</i> Adults tend to think kids have ulterior motives for doing relatively benign things. It&#39;s <i>possible</i> he simply enjoys his agency."},{"owner":{"account_id":22816296,"reputation":117,"user_id":42661,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://i.sstatic.net/z1N8tkx5.png?s=256","display_name":"Bentley Carpenter","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/42661/bentley-carpenter"},"edited":false,"score":3,"creation_date":1663159002,"post_id":42884,"comment_id":91740,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"Hello, welcome to Parenting SE! At the moment it is a little unclear to me as to what exactly do you want to do anyway. Are asking us how to make him want to be carried inside?"},{"owner":{"account_id":9081714,"reputation":131,"user_id":30236,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/5281737beac6876285062439d1f32e15?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG&f=y&so-version=2","display_name":"Ben","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/30236/ben"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1663169764,"post_id":42884,"comment_id":91741,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"Thank you, I was about to ask the exact same question with a 17 month old daughter."},{"owner":{"account_id":4570126,"reputation":81,"user_id":43487,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/56f91f29bcfc2a44b8a81eb010d67def?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG&f=y&so-version=2","display_name":"mamaLuss","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/43487/mamaluss"},"reply_to_user":{"account_id":22816296,"reputation":117,"user_id":42661,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://i.sstatic.net/z1N8tkx5.png?s=256","display_name":"Bentley Carpenter","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/42661/bentley-carpenter"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1663173842,"post_id":42884,"comment_id":91742,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"@BentleyCarpenter It would be nice if he could be playing inside a bit. I hear from my friends their kids are able to sit (as long as mom is talking to them), or just be on tummy and look around and be content. But when i try this with my son he starts being bored in few mins and shouting starts."},{"owner":{"account_id":26375403,"reputation":1,"user_id":43506,"user_type":"unregistered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/a9b31fe85d930fe2aa064c4b7c7105ea?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"Sarah","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/43506/sarah"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1663550252,"post_id":41819,"comment_id":91770,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"Oh my gosh we are going thru this exact same thing right now and my husband just asked me if I posted the original question. Did you get any real advice on how to handle in the moment? We do a lot of road trips and it is just constant. I am googling leg restraints for toddlers at this point."},{"owner":{"account_id":3674367,"reputation":72549,"user_id":9327,"user_type":"registered","accept_rate":50,"profile_image":"https://i.sstatic.net/jlp4Q.png?s=256","display_name":"anongoodnurse","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/9327/anongoodnurse"},"reply_to_user":{"account_id":26375403,"reputation":1,"user_id":43506,"user_type":"unregistered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/a9b31fe85d930fe2aa064c4b7c7105ea?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"Sarah","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/43506/sarah"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1663631624,"post_id":41819,"comment_id":91775,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"@Sarah - The Op replied in a comment to yours: &quot;Honestly, we started taking our 3 row vehicle more where it would separate our oldest and middle. Now if we were to take our vehicle where they are in a row together, he has mostly grown out of it but they do still argue more when they are next to each other (just not aggressive kicking). They are now 3 and 6.&quot;"},{"owner":{"account_id":4948536,"reputation":19410,"user_id":11249,"user_type":"moderator","profile_image":"https://i.sstatic.net/3RVO7.png?s=256","display_name":"Stephie","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/11249/stephie"},"edited":false,"score":2,"creation_date":1664022712,"post_id":42912,"comment_id":91797,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"Welcome! Have you seen the related Q/As in the topic? You could also find good suggestions there."},{"owner":{"account_id":1780022,"reputation":63542,"user_id":6524,"user_type":"registered","accept_rate":80,"profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/40931bddde219f1a9e4514d2f4cfa826?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"Joe","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/6524/joe"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1664904346,"post_id":42929,"comment_id":91822,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"How do you get meat in <i>your</i> diet?  What is your normal meal?"},{"owner":{"account_id":2516845,"reputation":2862,"user_id":9825,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/b01bd8a23b6e8bd0c02debddbea921ba?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"Zibbobz","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/9825/zibbobz"},"reply_to_user":{"account_id":1780022,"reputation":63542,"user_id":6524,"user_type":"registered","accept_rate":80,"profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/40931bddde219f1a9e4514d2f4cfa826?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"Joe","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/6524/joe"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1664907434,"post_id":42929,"comment_id":91823,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"@Joe We take turns preparing meals throughout the week, though some days neither of us are up for it and we either order out or bring food home from the store - but even on days like that, we still need to feed our son something healthy."},{"owner":{"account_id":1780022,"reputation":63542,"user_id":6524,"user_type":"registered","accept_rate":80,"profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/40931bddde219f1a9e4514d2f4cfa826?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"Joe","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/6524/joe"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1664907985,"post_id":42929,"comment_id":91824,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"Understood, but what is it that you are preparing or ordering?  Your question mostly eliminated the standard answers, so - what do you actually eat?"},{"owner":{"account_id":1780022,"reputation":63542,"user_id":6524,"user_type":"registered","accept_rate":80,"profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/40931bddde219f1a9e4514d2f4cfa826?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"Joe","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/6524/joe"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1664908186,"post_id":42929,"comment_id":91825,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"To put it a different way - one answer I might consider is &quot;feed them what you are eating&quot;.  Is that a possibility? Do you eat a balanced nutritious meal?  What foods are you eating?"},{"owner":{"account_id":2516845,"reputation":2862,"user_id":9825,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/b01bd8a23b6e8bd0c02debddbea921ba?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"Zibbobz","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/9825/zibbobz"},"reply_to_user":{"account_id":1780022,"reputation":63542,"user_id":6524,"user_type":"registered","accept_rate":80,"profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/40931bddde219f1a9e4514d2f4cfa826?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"Joe","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/6524/joe"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1664909142,"post_id":42929,"comment_id":91826,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"@Joe I guess my answer to that is, under normal circumstances we try to feed him the same things we&#39;re eating, but we try to prepare it with less sodium.  It&#39;s okay if we have a few meals that aren&#39;t perfect, but we don&#39;t want to feed our son too much sodium-loaded food. When he&#39;s a bit older, takeout food and quick meals occasionally might be okay. But he&#39;s only one year old right now and he needs good nutrition."},{"owner":{"account_id":1780022,"reputation":63542,"user_id":6524,"user_type":"registered","accept_rate":80,"profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/40931bddde219f1a9e4514d2f4cfa826?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"Joe","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/6524/joe"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1664928501,"post_id":42929,"comment_id":91827,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"You&#39;re still not answering my question.  What foods do you eat?  What was your dinner yesterday? Day before that?  Breakfast?  How are we supposed to talk about how you can feed your infant appropriately if we don&#39;t know what <i>you</i> eat?"},{"owner":{"account_id":3674367,"reputation":72549,"user_id":9327,"user_type":"registered","accept_rate":50,"profile_image":"https://i.sstatic.net/jlp4Q.png?s=256","display_name":"anongoodnurse","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/9327/anongoodnurse"},"reply_to_user":{"account_id":1780022,"reputation":63542,"user_id":6524,"user_type":"registered","accept_rate":80,"profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/40931bddde219f1a9e4514d2f4cfa826?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"Joe","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/6524/joe"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1664930131,"post_id":42929,"comment_id":91828,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"@Joe - The OP has expressed what he thinks is an answer, and I see it. Presume that the OP wants to feed the child differently than they feed themselves. It&#39;s been asked and answered."},{"owner":{"account_id":3674367,"reputation":72549,"user_id":9327,"user_type":"registered","accept_rate":50,"profile_image":"https://i.sstatic.net/jlp4Q.png?s=256","display_name":"anongoodnurse","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/9327/anongoodnurse"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1664930287,"post_id":42929,"comment_id":91829,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"Do you bake? Do you use your freezer? We&#39;re happy to help, but how much do you know about nutrition? We can help you sneak in healthy foods if you <i>know</i> what healthy foods are. :)"},{"owner":{"account_id":2516845,"reputation":2862,"user_id":9825,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/b01bd8a23b6e8bd0c02debddbea921ba?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"Zibbobz","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/9825/zibbobz"},"edited":false,"score":1,"creation_date":1664974722,"post_id":42929,"comment_id":91830,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"We do bake, and we do make things like baby-safe stir fry vegetables, soups that we can easily puree for him, spaghetti that we can cut up for him, and other stuff that&#39;s generally okay for him to eat - I&#39;m more concerned with nights where we <i>don&#39;t</i> feel like cooking at all, and either order out some pizza/sushi/chinese, but still need to make something for our son."},{"owner":{"account_id":9754817,"reputation":2492,"user_id":42067,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/e8983c003003ba97dc6398b3be5b5bb3?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG&f=y&so-version=2","display_name":"R Davies","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/42067/r-davies"},"edited":false,"score":1,"creation_date":1664979049,"post_id":42929,"comment_id":91832,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"I happily feed my son pizza/sushi/Chinese occasionally, as the rest of his diet has very little salt in it!"},{"owner":{"account_id":2516845,"reputation":2862,"user_id":9825,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/b01bd8a23b6e8bd0c02debddbea921ba?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"Zibbobz","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/9825/zibbobz"},"reply_to_user":{"account_id":9754817,"reputation":2492,"user_id":42067,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/e8983c003003ba97dc6398b3be5b5bb3?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG&f=y&so-version=2","display_name":"R Davies","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/42067/r-davies"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1664990327,"post_id":42929,"comment_id":91835,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"@RDavies If that is your answer, it would honestly be appreciated.  A lot of the reason I&#39;m asking this right now is anxiety over the idea of feeding my son an inappropriate diet because of our takeout habits, so if the answer is &quot;it&#39;s actually fine to do that sometimes&quot;, it would be a reassuring thing to hear."},{"owner":{"account_id":6833993,"reputation":1782,"user_id":17701,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/171c374849c84ee6fa29f2130a0b4212?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG&f=y&so-version=2","display_name":"iulia","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/17701/iulia"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1664992541,"post_id":42929,"comment_id":91836,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"Why not legumes for protein? Soak over night and boil for 10-20 minutes in a pressure cooker."},{"owner":{"account_id":2516845,"reputation":2862,"user_id":9825,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/b01bd8a23b6e8bd0c02debddbea921ba?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"Zibbobz","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/9825/zibbobz"},"reply_to_user":{"account_id":6833993,"reputation":1782,"user_id":17701,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/171c374849c84ee6fa29f2130a0b4212?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG&f=y&so-version=2","display_name":"iulia","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/17701/iulia"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1665060426,"post_id":42929,"comment_id":91838,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"@iulia A 24-hour prep time is absolutely not what I&#39;m looking for in this circumstance - I&#39;m more looking for something I can make quickly without having to prepare ahead of time for it."},{"owner":{"account_id":6833993,"reputation":1782,"user_id":17701,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/171c374849c84ee6fa29f2130a0b4212?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG&f=y&so-version=2","display_name":"iulia","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/17701/iulia"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1665247362,"post_id":42929,"comment_id":91843,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"@Zibbobz There is also the option of canned beans (preferably with no/low added salt). Legumes are a great source of protein and it would add variety in your child&#39;s diet (and your own, of course). <a href=\"https://www.healthline.com/nutrition/are-canned-beans-healthy#benefits\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">healthline.com/nutrition/are-canned-beans-healthy#benefits</a>"},{"owner":{"account_id":2067036,"reputation":8662,"user_id":3527,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/27caf1b4834e7f79a4bc8af5890424ba?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"Hilmar","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/3527/hilmar"},"edited":false,"score":3,"creation_date":1666108796,"post_id":42951,"comment_id":91881,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"Almost all TV these days comes with safety straps so you can tie to the wall or another stable object behind it."},{"owner":{"account_id":1376814,"reputation":101,"user_id":43617,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://i.sstatic.net/XAb54.png?s=256","display_name":"Arnaud Bouchot","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/43617/arnaud-bouchot"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1666259002,"post_id":42951,"comment_id":91913,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"Defo strap it, it will prevent the TV to tilt and fall but it won&#39;t shield it from flying objects like it happened to ours &lt;crack&gt;. You could still get a screen protector fitted until your son makes sense of &quot;no&quot; but that defeats the purpose of having a nice TV as it will look ugly and alter the picture quality"},{"owner":{"account_id":5748511,"reputation":101,"user_id":43627,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/f681d3b7bbad816f3ff0de72acfc50d7?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG&f=y&so-version=2","display_name":"Rohat Kılı&#231;","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/43627/rohat-k%c4%b1l%c4%b1%c3%a7"},"edited":false,"score":1,"creation_date":1666279270,"post_id":42951,"comment_id":91915,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"By TV-proofing your 10-mo-old baby."},{"owner":{"account_id":8643622,"reputation":544,"user_id":25616,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/255c7474b350b0e2630fc7093e077a7f?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG&f=y&so-version=2","display_name":"Robert Columbia","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/25616/robert-columbia"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1666298000,"post_id":42737,"comment_id":91917,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"This is a really interesting question, phrased well for a hot-button topic, and something that occurred to me after binging on Law and Order: SVU. Considering the well-known phenomenon of infantile amnesia, query whether someone would have any specific memories of touching at all. Even without specific memory, could it result in more generalized emotional dysregulation lasting into later life (e.g. an adult had emotional troubles, but has no idea it was caused by CSA because they don&#39;t remember any CSA)?"},{"owner":{"user_type":"does_not_exist","display_name":"user43641"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1666381300,"post_id":42951,"comment_id":91931,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"I can&#39;t answer without 10 rep. Large baby pen on amazon. As they get older everything in the house &quot;moves up&quot; to keep out of hands reach... but right around the time they&#39;re crawling to learning to walk well, its impossible to keep them out of everything all the time and a large 6x7 foot pen has helped. Toys go in the pen, and siblings and parents too.  And yes please make sure the TV wont topple now, before you forget."},{"owner":{"account_id":20662335,"reputation":444,"user_id":43628,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/7d7f4dbddcc90d59d8466b313fb10c0a?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG&f=y&so-version=2","display_name":"Ilianna","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/43628/ilianna"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1667311742,"post_id":43015,"comment_id":92054,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"You said the trip is about 350 miles away, but how long is that in minutes/hours? Whats the total amount of time the trip would take you?"},{"owner":{"account_id":2516845,"reputation":2862,"user_id":9825,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/b01bd8a23b6e8bd0c02debddbea921ba?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"Zibbobz","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/9825/zibbobz"},"reply_to_user":{"account_id":20662335,"reputation":444,"user_id":43628,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/7d7f4dbddcc90d59d8466b313fb10c0a?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG&f=y&so-version=2","display_name":"Ilianna","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/43628/ilianna"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1667328982,"post_id":43015,"comment_id":92056,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"@Ilianna Added this information."},{"owner":{"account_id":2972157,"reputation":101,"user_id":43696,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/773a49a9b40f41e0661c032a26197467?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"undershock","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/43696/undershock"},"edited":false,"score":4,"creation_date":1667341384,"post_id":43015,"comment_id":92059,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"I&#39;ve never been on Amtrak, but I have been with a 15 month old on a long distance London to Edinburgh here in the UK (332 miles).  It is a long journey, but one of the advantages of a train is, like a flight during the cruising phase, you&#39;re pretty much free to wonder about and unlike driving you can interact/play with your child. There&#39;s substantially more space than a flight though and you&#39;re less likely to get in the way!"},{"owner":{"account_id":23898455,"reputation":111,"user_id":43611,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/5303e16ee7aa9b0d884d6b464bc06e60?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG&f=y&so-version=2","display_name":"Bri Han","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/43611/bri-han"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1667392912,"post_id":43000,"comment_id":92065,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"Even though it has been 4 weeks, this could still be a sign of teething. Is he showing any other signs? Or just drooling?"},{"owner":{"account_id":2516845,"reputation":2862,"user_id":9825,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/b01bd8a23b6e8bd0c02debddbea921ba?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"Zibbobz","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/9825/zibbobz"},"reply_to_user":{"account_id":2972157,"reputation":101,"user_id":43696,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/773a49a9b40f41e0661c032a26197467?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"undershock","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/43696/undershock"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1667406894,"post_id":43015,"comment_id":92068,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"@undershock There is the issue with other passengers and the motion of the train possibly being a bit off-putting to the child, but hopefully we can just keep close to him and comfort him as need be."},{"owner":{"account_id":85750,"reputation":1992,"user_id":16114,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/8ca29123b5669b26f9b6ca2c62d9d215?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"Wayne Conrad","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/16114/wayne-conrad"},"edited":false,"score":1,"creation_date":1667410961,"post_id":43015,"comment_id":92071,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"@Zibbobz There is also the possibility that motion of the train may lure your child to sleep."},{"owner":{"account_id":20662335,"reputation":444,"user_id":43628,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/7d7f4dbddcc90d59d8466b313fb10c0a?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG&f=y&so-version=2","display_name":"Ilianna","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/43628/ilianna"},"reply_to_user":{"account_id":23898455,"reputation":111,"user_id":43611,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/5303e16ee7aa9b0d884d6b464bc06e60?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG&f=y&so-version=2","display_name":"Bri Han","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/43611/bri-han"},"edited":false,"score":1,"creation_date":1667569223,"post_id":43000,"comment_id":92085,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"@BriHan Drooling and putting his hands in his mouth!"},{"owner":{"account_id":20553,"reputation":10800,"user_id":7798,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/431cd43aaf713caa80316e852a87a840?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"Paul Johnson","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/7798/paul-johnson"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1668379079,"post_id":43047,"comment_id":92122,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"I&#39;m sorry, but I&#39;ve voted to close due to lack of focus. I can see you are looking for guidance about what you can and can&#39;t safely do when breast-feeding, but this is just too general. There just so many things a mother can do, or be exposed to, and some of them can affect the baby via her milk or by other routes. But there is no way we can list everything. Can you narrow it down a bit?"},{"owner":{"account_id":3086412,"reputation":119,"user_id":43737,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/3c38224dffaa2d7383314284038f9c26?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"sid-m","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/43737/sid-m"},"reply_to_user":{"account_id":20553,"reputation":10800,"user_id":7798,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/431cd43aaf713caa80316e852a87a840?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"Paul Johnson","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/7798/paul-johnson"},"edited":false,"score":1,"creation_date":1668393992,"post_id":43047,"comment_id":92123,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"Thanks. But actually I am not looking for a guidance about what can or can&#39;t be done safely while breast-feeding. I just want simple &quot;yes&quot; or &quot;no&quot; answers based on knowledge/experiences to confirm whether or not this is possible. Because there is a disagreement between me and my wife about this."},{"owner":{"account_id":3674367,"reputation":72549,"user_id":9327,"user_type":"registered","accept_rate":50,"profile_image":"https://i.sstatic.net/jlp4Q.png?s=256","display_name":"anongoodnurse","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/9327/anongoodnurse"},"edited":false,"score":1,"creation_date":1668987734,"post_id":43053,"comment_id":92133,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"Hi and welcome! Is your son wearing a diaper to bed? If so, have you tried switching to a more absorbent diaper? I&#39;m not sure I understand your general concern."},{"owner":{"account_id":7939571,"reputation":13,"user_id":43724,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://i.sstatic.net/Oni5t.jpg?s=256","display_name":"comand","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/43724/comand"},"reply_to_user":{"account_id":3674367,"reputation":72549,"user_id":9327,"user_type":"registered","accept_rate":50,"profile_image":"https://i.sstatic.net/jlp4Q.png?s=256","display_name":"anongoodnurse","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/9327/anongoodnurse"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1669010556,"post_id":43053,"comment_id":92134,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"thank you :) yes, he is wearing a diaper, and we did! actually it was the first thing we did. i understand the confusion, my question is how can we help him to stop wetting the bed?"},{"owner":{"account_id":4948536,"reputation":19410,"user_id":11249,"user_type":"moderator","profile_image":"https://i.sstatic.net/3RVO7.png?s=256","display_name":"Stephie","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/11249/stephie"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1669757194,"post_id":43076,"comment_id":92176,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"Are you eating together as a family, or is he given his foods separately?"},{"owner":{"account_id":408021,"reputation":285,"user_id":13478,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://i.sstatic.net/oyv6J.png?s=256","display_name":"KRyan","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/13478/kryan"},"reply_to_user":{"account_id":4948536,"reputation":19410,"user_id":11249,"user_type":"moderator","profile_image":"https://i.sstatic.net/3RVO7.png?s=256","display_name":"Stephie","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/11249/stephie"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1669757440,"post_id":43076,"comment_id":92177,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"@Stephie Generally not literally simultaneously, since feeding him—even offering him the food—requires us to assist (e.g. pick up thrown or dropped food or utensils), which prevents us from eating at the same time. But often his eating is just before or just after ours, and we all sit together through both our meals and his."},{"owner":{"account_id":9754817,"reputation":2492,"user_id":42067,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/e8983c003003ba97dc6398b3be5b5bb3?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG&f=y&so-version=2","display_name":"R Davies","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/42067/r-davies"},"edited":false,"score":2,"creation_date":1669797859,"post_id":43076,"comment_id":92178,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"could it be teething? how is he with his mouth the rest of the time?"},{"owner":{"account_id":408021,"reputation":285,"user_id":13478,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://i.sstatic.net/oyv6J.png?s=256","display_name":"KRyan","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/13478/kryan"},"reply_to_user":{"account_id":9754817,"reputation":2492,"user_id":42067,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/e8983c003003ba97dc6398b3be5b5bb3?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG&f=y&so-version=2","display_name":"R Davies","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/42067/r-davies"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1669819672,"post_id":43076,"comment_id":92180,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"@RDavies I mean, teething is pretty obviously a factor in general, and he definitely has some discomfort there. But we haven’t otherwise observed it getting <i>worse</i> during this timespan, so I’m not convinced it’s the full story? Then again, last night he happily ate his dinner with great enthusiasm and actually probably swallowed a good chunk of it, with no apparent changes on our part, so who knows. Still interested in learning if there are any suggestions for this, in case that was a one-off."},{"owner":{"account_id":15284488,"reputation":291,"user_id":36356,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/238a4bb1241086158ec0cd2fe10250ad?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG&f=y&so-version=2","display_name":"Allerleirauh","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/36356/allerleirauh"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1669874543,"post_id":43076,"comment_id":92182,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"In general: Do you visit some doctor with your son regularly? (Here in Germany, there were scheduled visits by age, ie 2 month, 6 month, 10 month or similar to make sure the child evolves healthy). You could let the doctor check next time the throat and mouth to be safe there is no physical reason for the crying."},{"owner":{"account_id":408021,"reputation":285,"user_id":13478,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://i.sstatic.net/oyv6J.png?s=256","display_name":"KRyan","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/13478/kryan"},"reply_to_user":{"account_id":15284488,"reputation":291,"user_id":36356,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/238a4bb1241086158ec0cd2fe10250ad?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG&f=y&so-version=2","display_name":"Allerleirauh","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/36356/allerleirauh"},"edited":false,"score":1,"creation_date":1669875011,"post_id":43076,"comment_id":92183,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"@Allerleirauh Of course, and he does have an appointment coming up where we’ll ask. I’d be surprised if there is any physical reason, though—he very happily puts plenty of non-food items in his mouth (teethers, plushes, plastic or wooden toys... if we’d let him, TV remotes, glasses, hair...), plus as I said, the night I asked this question and the following night (today) were no-fuss, even swallowed a certain amount as far as we can tell."},{"owner":{"account_id":2908815,"reputation":101,"user_id":43838,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://i.sstatic.net/hu1K8.png?s=256","display_name":"Mackie","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/43838/mackie"},"edited":false,"score":1,"creation_date":1671014677,"post_id":43053,"comment_id":92204,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"Hello, my daughter is almost 3 years old and still wearing diaper at night (not at daytime). My son is almost 5 and stopped wearing diaper at night a few month ago (so a little bit more than 4 and a half). I think this is normal."},{"owner":{"account_id":2908815,"reputation":101,"user_id":43838,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://i.sstatic.net/hu1K8.png?s=256","display_name":"Mackie","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/43838/mackie"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1672735180,"post_id":43053,"comment_id":92241,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"@comand: If you find my comment helpful, could you please give it an upvote? Thank you :-)"},{"owner":{"account_id":2208996,"reputation":101,"user_id":44004,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://www.gravatar.com/avatar/5cc705a3347fbe7b34982782b6f702a0?s=256&d=identicon&r=PG","display_name":"nadapez","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/44004/nadapez"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1674213714,"post_id":41610,"comment_id":92413,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"This is about parenting children, not grondmothers . But do the same with her. Call her good girl each time she does something good and she will be aware of how silly feels that"},{"owner":{"account_id":14511655,"reputation":1509,"user_id":33359,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://i.sstatic.net/k3ikS5b8.jpg?s=256","display_name":"elbrant","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/33359/elbrant"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1675528885,"post_id":42221,"comment_id":92565,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"Has your daughter ever used a pacifier?"},{"owner":{"account_id":12748328,"reputation":101,"user_id":44790,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://i.sstatic.net/WFcUW.png?s=256","display_name":"Nikki","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/44790/nikki"},"edited":false,"score":1,"creation_date":1690456291,"post_id":42221,"comment_id":93247,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"This question was asked 20 months ago. I wonder if, now the child is almost 4 years old, the situation resolved itself and your daughter is now fit an healthy? What was it you did to resolve this issue, other than just giving her time to grow out of the behaviour?"},{"owner":{"account_id":1455416,"reputation":266,"user_id":44867,"user_type":"registered","profile_image":"https://i.sstatic.net/5TMeZ.jpg?s=256","display_name":"Dennis Hackethal","link":"https://parenting.stackexchange.com/users/44867/dennis-hackethal"},"edited":false,"score":0,"creation_date":1691854668,"post_id":42060,"comment_id":93441,"content_license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","body":"&quot;But as soon as his hands and feet touch the mattress, his legs start to kick in the air and his hands and arms start to swing about [...].&quot; Have you considered that he&#39;s doing this because he does not want to go to bed yet? In which case you wouldn&#39;t be <i>helping</i> him settle. Sometimes I&#39;m sleepy or just look sleepy but don&#39;t feel like sleeping yet."}],"has_more":false,"quota_max":300,"quota_remaining":272}